// The loop over the blocks of blake3_servil_avx512_p32 (../../../kcheck/b3hashr.o), for the prover of the
// verifier in Lean. As in p16.places the place is at the loop's bottom: a block has just been compressed in
// every lane; `left` is the count of blocks still to do, the block just done counted in it; the next block,
// if there is one, lies 64 bytes after `off`.
//
// This kernel has thirty-two lanes: lane i of zmm0 to zmm7 is the chunk of inputs[i], and lane i of zmm8 to
// zmm15 the chunk of inputs[i + 16].
//
// It keeps four vectors in cells of its frame for the whole loop, and reads them back in each turn: the low
// and the high words of the counter, once for each half of the lanes. A `cell` line says what such a cell
// holds, word by word.
//
// The two facts of `end` and of `length` are there for the verifier: this kernel works out the last block's
// flags and its length only where the block is the last, and what the lanes are said to hold names both. A
// fact that names a number makes the verifier work it out on every path that comes to the place.
place +0xf44 {
    name left = r13
    name off = r14
    fact left >= 1
    fact left <= n
    fact off == 64 * (n - left)
    fact end <= 255
    fact length <= 255
    lane i: zmm0 .. zmm7 = chunk(key, t, flags, start, end, length, n, inputs[i]) after n - left + 1
    lane i: zmm8 .. zmm15 = chunk(key, t, flags, start, end, length, n, inputs[i + 16]) after n - left + 1
    cell [rsp + 2048]: word i = lo(t)
    cell [rsp + 2112]: word i = hi(t)
    cell [rsp + 2176]: word i = lo(t)
    cell [rsp + 2240]: word i = hi(t)
    decreases left
}
